{"archetypes":[{"name":"quiet-fd-routing","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Verifies internal consistency of the 'no raw >&2 in lib' invariant against emit_failed_agent_stderr_tail_raw, and confirms each caller's quiet-init classification matches the plan's assumptions.","prompt_body":"The plan asserts lib-failed-agent-stderr-tail.sh performs 'NO raw >&2' so it is safe to source from quiet-init callers, yet also defines `emit_failed_agent_stderr_tail_raw` which uses `printf >&2` — the plan resolves this by restricting that function to run-external-agent.sh only, which 'has no quiet-init.' Read run-external-agent.sh to confirm it does not source lib-quiet.sh (making the `>&2` call safe there). Read launch-claude-subprocess.sh and launch-claude-review.sh to confirm they are quiet-init callers and the plan never directs them to call `emit_failed_agent_stderr_tail_raw` (only `write_failed_agent_stderr_tail`, which the plan claims avoids raw >&2). Investigate whether the lint rule `lint-no-raw-stderr-after-quiet-init` scans all code transitively reachable from a sourced file, or only top-level lines — if it scans the lib body, the presence of `emit_failed_agent_stderr_tail_raw` could trigger a false positive even though quiet-init callers never invoke that function. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"collector-dedup-alignment","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks plan's dedup insertion point comment, per-slot variable names, retry sidecar naming pattern, and larch_err availability against the actual collect-agent-results.sh structure.","prompt_body":"The plan inserts a dedup-emit pass 'immediately before `# --- 4. Emit structured results ---`' in collect-agent-results.sh — read that file to verify this section comment exists at the claimed location and that the plan's claimed ordering (after sections 3–3.7 mutations complete) matches the actual code structure. The dedup logic references `REVIEWER_FILE`, `TOOL`, `STATUS`, and `ORIG_OUTPUT` as per-slot tracking variables — verify these exact names exist and hold the claimed values at the proposed insertion point in the existing retry and result-tracking code. Check the retry sidecar path: the plan uses `${REVIEWER_FILE%.txt}-retry.txt.stderr-tail` as the preferred path when a retry happened — confirm retry output files are actually named with this pattern in the existing code and that `REVIEWER_FILE` points to the original (not retry) path when a retry has completed so the suffix-strip resolves correctly. Verify that `larch_err` is available in collect-agent-results.sh without additional sourcing beyond the already-present lib-quiet.sh. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"source-selection-mapping","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Verifies that the plan's sidecar/diag/output source-selection priority order for run-external-agent.sh accurately maps to what each capture mode actually writes at non-zero exit.","prompt_body":"The plan specifies a source-selection priority order for failed runs in run-external-agent.sh: first `${OUTPUT_FILE}.sidecar`, then `${OUTPUT_FILE}.diag`, then `${OUTPUT_FILE}` itself — read the FAILED branch (~lines 289-299) and TIMED_OUT branch (~lines 250-265) to confirm which file actually contains stderr at each exit point for each capture mode (`--capture-stdout-only`, default sidecar mode, `--capture-stdout` merged). Check whether the TIMED_OUT branch populates the same files as a clean non-zero FAILED exit — a timed-out codex/cursor run may not have flushed `.sidecar` content yet, making the source-selection order behave differently from what the plan describes. Verify the plan's coverage claim for the claude lane: launch-claude-subprocess.sh writes stderr to `${OUTPUT_CANON}.stderr`, but the plan's source-selection order for run-external-agent.sh lists `.sidecar`, `.diag`, and the main output — confirm whether claude agent invocations are routed through run-external-agent.sh at all, or whether they bypass it entirely (making the source-selection irrelevant for that lane). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
